        "original_id": "5fb9349b-5bb4-5dbc-8724-5004449f9d3a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim Burton, Jon Peters, Peter Guber, Prince\n- Works: Batman (1989 film), Batdance, Kiss\n- Organizations: DC Comics, Mandalay Entertainment\n- Topics: film production, music charts\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Prince's song \"Kiss\" was the last of his songs before \"Batdance\" to top all three American charts.\n- Batman is a 1989 American superhero film based on the DC Comics character Batman.\n- Batman was directed by Tim Burton and produced by Jon Peters and Peter Guber.\n- Peter Guber is Chairman and CEO of Mandalay Entertainment.\n- Helped by the popularity of the film Batman, Prince's song \"Batdance\" reached number one in the United States.\n- \"Batdance\" became Prince's fourth American number-one single and his first since \"Kiss\" in 1986 to top all three American charts.",
